at\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" from\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" form\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\".rkt\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" example\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\", how to validate non\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"-empty? Let me check the\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" con\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"script-reference\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" for the `@\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"form` widget\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" and `\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"~error`. Let me look\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" at the intro\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" part\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" of con\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"script-reference to\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" see the simple\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" form handling\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\".\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"bash:8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"@form\\|defstep\\|defstudy\\|defvar\\|skip\\|~error\" /workspace/../reference/congame-doc/conscript-reference.scrbl | head -40"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"bash:9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 400,520p /workspace/../reference/congame-doc/conscript-reference.scrbl"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"moonshotai/kimi-k3","usage":{"input":2005,"output":239,"cacheRead":3072,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":108,"totalTokens":5316,"cost":{"input":0.006015,"output":0.003585,"cacheRead":0.0009216,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0105216}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1792050727288,"responseId":"gen-1792050727-6d3rWOflEwn1pOAKLuOl","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"bash:8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"11:                              defstep\n12:                              defstep/study\n13:                              defstudy\n66:@defform[(defstep (step-id) step-body)]{\n68:@margin-note{For examples of @racket[defstep] in use, see @secref[\"intro\"].}\n75:@defform[(defstep/study step-id #:study child-study-expr\n95:included for compatibility. Use @racket[defvar*] and @racket[defvar*/instance] to share study\n102:         (defstudy study-id\n131:with @racket[defstep] or @racket[defstep/study].\n141:(defstudy college-try\n154:(defstudy mystudy\n158:(defstudy mystudy\n166:(defstudy repeating-step-study\n174:_step}] form. The @racket[_step-id-expr] is evaluated once, when the @racket[defstudy] form itself\n176:given to @racket[defstep/study], where each participant's child study can give the same step a\n180:(defstep/study run-task\n184:            (defstudy task-then-payment\n197:A @racket[defstudy] at the top level of a module evaluates @racket[_step-id-expr] once, when the\n198:module loads. A @racket[defstudy] inside a @racket[defstep/study] procedure evaluates it each time\n207:(defstudy retry-study\n217:@inline-note[#:type 'warning]{@racket[defstudy] cannot check runtime IDs when your module compiles.\n224:compatibility. Use @racket[defvar*] and @racket[defvar*/instance] to share study variables between\n294:(defstep (start)\n308:    (defstep (hello)\n310:    (defstudy s\n334:As with @racket[defstep], the @racket[_body] of a @racket[defview] expression should evaluate to a\n353:@racket[defstep].\n363:Returns a procedure, suitable for use with the @racket[#:wrapper] argument of @racket[defstudy],\n370:Returns a procedure, suitable for use with the @racket[#:wrapper] argument of @racket[defstudy],\n404:@racket[get-step-timings] directly within the body of a @racket[defstep] (outside of an action\n443:(defstep (age-name-survey)\n447:    @form{\n551:(defstep (start)\n556:(defstudy my-study\n737:Returns two values: a @formform value and a procedure that is called when the form is submitted.\n739:Each @racket[_id] should be a variable declared with @racket[defvar] or similar, and each\n745:(defvar my-name)\n746:(defvar my-middle-name)\n747:(defvar my-age)\n800:(defvar taste)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792050729914},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"bash:9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"See @secref[\"cookbook-step-timings\"] for an example showing how to use @racket[get-step-timings].\n\n@inline-note[#:type 'warning]{@bold{Important:} This function should @italic{only} be called within\na @racket[button]'s action procedure or within code that runs after a form is submitted. Calling\n@racket[get-step-timings] directly within the body of a @racket[defstep] (outside of an action\nprocedure) will return @racket[(cons #f #f)] because the timing data is only available when\nprocessing user actions like button clicks or form submissions.}\n\n}\n\n@;------------------------------------------------\n\n@subsection{Logging}\n\n@deftogether[(\n@defform*[[(log-conscript-debug string-expr)\n           (log-conscript-debug format-string-expr v ...)]]\n@defform*[[(log-conscript-info string-expr)\n           (log-conscript-info format-string-expr v ...)]]\n@defform*[[(log-conscript-warning string-expr)\n           (log-conscript-warning format-string-expr v ...)]]\n@defform*[[(log-conscript-error string-expr)\n           (log-conscript-error format-string-expr v ...)]]\n@defform*[[(log-conscript-fatal string-expr)\n           (log-conscript-fatal format-string-expr v ...)]])]{\n\n@margin-note{See @secref[\"logging\" #:doc '(lib \"scribblings/reference/reference.scrbl\")] in the\n@italic{Racket Reference} for more information on logging.}\n\nLogs an event with the Conscript logger, evaluating @racket[string-expr] or @racket[(format\nformat-string-expr v ...)]. These forms are listed above in order of severity.\n\nLogging functions are useful for debugging: for example, when you want to capture and surface\nstate information in the middle of a process, or extra context about possible causes of a problem.\n\nLogged events are printed on the console (@tt{stderr}) of a running Congame server.\n\nNote that since the result of a @racketkeywordfont{log-conscript-}@racket[_level] form is\n@|void-const|, you can't use it directly inside a study step. Instead, wrap it in a\n@racket[begin] expression that returns an empty string:\n\n@codeblock[#:keep-lang-line? #f]|{\n#lang conscript\n(defstep (age-name-survey)\n  @md{\n    # Survey\n\n    @form{\n      What is your first name? @(set! first-name (input-text))\n\n      @(begin\n        (log-conscript-info \"Hello\")\n        \"\")\n      @submit-button\n  }})\n}|\n\n}\n\n@screenshot{ref-log-example-output.png}\n\n\n@;------------------------------------------------\n\n@subsection{Boxes}\n\n\n@defform[(defbox id)]{\n\nDefines two functions, @racketkeywordfont{get-}@racket[_id] (which takes no arguments and returns\nthe value of @racket[_id]) and @racketkeywordfont{set!-}@racket[_id] (which takes one argument and\nupdates the value of @racket[_id]).\n\n@examples[#:eval e\n(define flux 81)\n(defbox flux)\n(get-flux)\n(set!-flux \"new\")\n(get-flux)\nflux\n\n]\n\n}\n\n@subsubsection{Additional box functions}\n\n@declare-exporting[conscript/var-box conscript/base]\n@defmodule[conscript/var-box #:no-declare]\n\nThe bindings from this module are also provided by @racketmodname[conscript/base].\n\n@defform[(define-var-box id var)]{\n\nBinds @racket[_id] to a function that can take zero arguments or one argument. If given no\narguments, the function returns the current value of @racket[_var] (which must already be defined\nelsewhere); if given a single argument, the function @racket[set!]s the value of @racket[_var] to\nthat value.\n\nThe function @racket[_id] can be passed to other functions, allowing them to access or update a\nlocal variable.\n\n@examples[#:eval e\n(define flux #f)\n(define-var-box get-or-set flux)\n\n(get-or-set)\n(get-or-set 'foo)\n(get-or-set)\nflux\n]\n\n}\n\n\n@;~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n@; @subsection{Local Testing}\n\n@; @defmodulelang[conscript/local]\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1792050729914},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The simple style `(set! first-name (input-text))` inside `@form` is convenient. For non-empty validation, I can use `ensure` with `required`? But in this simpler `@form` (the congame form style without form0), the input-text is a widget whose binding gets set directly. Validation in that style... Let me check how `@form` in conscript/base works — grep for \"defproc[(form\" in conscript source, or look at the doc around line 973 for input-text and the form from congame/components/study.\n\nActually there's a simpler approach: use `defvar` + `@form` with `(set! name (input-text))`, and check in the transition: if name is empty, go back to the form step with an error message. But simplest: use form0's `form+submit` with `required` validator which gives automatic error message re-rendering. That requires `conscript/form0` require. Let's check `defvar` semantics and the `form` render approach. The doc example at line ~745 shows form+submit. And `@rw[\"name\" (input-text \"Name\")]` render style.\n\nLet me write:\n\n```racket\n#lang conscript\n\n(require conscript/form0)\n\n(provide benchmark-study)\n\n(defvar display-name)\n\n(defstep (intro)\n  @md{# Welcome\n      This is a short study. Click Continue to begin.\n      @button{Continue}})\n\n(define-values (name-form on-submit)\n  (form+submit\n   [display-name (ensure binding/text (required))]))\n\n(defstep (get-name)\n  (define (render rw)\n    @md{# Your Name\n        @rw[\"display-name\" (input-text \"Display name:\")]\n        @|submit-button|})\n  @md{@form[name-form on-submit render]})\n\n(defstep (final)\n  @md{# Thank You\n      Thanks, @display-name, for participating.})\n\n(defstudy benchmark-study\n  [intro --> get-name --> final]\n  [final --> final])\n```\n\nWait — `required` validator: does it treat empty string as missing? In forms library, `required` ensures value is present (not #f). An empty text input submits empty string \"\" — binding/text gives \"\" not #f? Let me check the forms library. The `required` validator from forms: \"ensures a value is present (i.e. not #f)\". Empty string from text input... Let me check the forms package binding/text: it produces the string; empty input produces \"\"? Actually in the forms library, binding/text on missing field gives #f. An empty text input in browser submits the field with empty value, so binding is present with \"\". Hmm, but forms library's `required` validator may check `non-empty-string?`? Let me look at the source.\n\nLet me check the forms collection installed.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" simple style\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\" `(\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"set\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"! first-name (input-text\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"))` inside\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0},{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\